\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces The $30$ published pairs summarized in Table~\ref {tab:scatter}, with the reported gain of the system over the baseline in percentage points and the paper and table that report it. R@$k$: passage recall@$k$. EM: exact match of one reader given each system's retrieval. Hit(s)@1: accuracy of the top-ranked answer entity. Evidence recall: GraphRAG-Bench's Novel subset, Complex Reasoning questions. TF--IDF + BM25: TF--IDF article retrieval followed by BM25 passage ranking. Text only: the same model with a text corpus in place of the KB. MoR takes its BM25 rows from \citet  {wu2024stark}; the GraftNet and KV-Mem rows are PullNet's reproductions. Structure: the benchmark's own source KB; a graph the system builds from the corpus (corpus-built); or Wikipedia passages linked through Wikidata.}}{27}{table.caption.51}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:pairs}{{17}{27}{The $30$ published pairs summarized in Table~\ref {tab:scatter}, with the reported gain of the system over the baseline in percentage points and the paper and table that report it. R@$k$: passage recall@$k$. EM: exact match of one reader given each system's retrieval. Hit(s)@1: accuracy of the top-ranked answer entity. Evidence recall: GraphRAG-Bench's Novel subset, Complex Reasoning questions. TF--IDF + BM25: TF--IDF article retrieval followed by BM25 passage ranking. Text only: the same model with a text corpus in place of the KB. MoR takes its BM25 rows from \citet {wu2024stark}; the GraftNet and KV-Mem rows are PullNet's reproductions. Structure: the benchmark's own source KB; a graph the system builds from the corpus (corpus-built); or Wikipedia passages linked through Wikidata}{table.caption.51}{}}
