\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Cross-retriever replication of the 2WikiMultiHop swap on a pure PPR retriever and a hybrid-PPR variant: the effect persists and is larger for the PPR-based retrievers than for the hybrid retriever. Each row gives the mean paired hit@5 difference, aligned KG minus independent OpenIE KG, with its $10{,}000$-resample bootstrap $95\%$ CI, for the hybrid retriever of \S  \ref {sec:setup}, a pure PPR retriever, and a hybrid-PPR variant whose ranking is carried by a PPR channel, on the first and held-out $200$-question splits of inference questions and the $200$-question compositional split. The largest swap effect on each kind of split is in \textbf  {bold}.}}{34}{table.caption.63}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:swapreplication}{{23}{34}{Cross-retriever replication of the 2WikiMultiHop swap on a pure PPR retriever and a hybrid-PPR variant: the effect persists and is larger for the PPR-based retrievers than for the hybrid retriever. Each row gives the mean paired hit@5 difference, aligned KG minus independent OpenIE KG, with its $10{,}000$-resample bootstrap $95\%$ CI, for the hybrid retriever of \S \ref {sec:setup}, a pure PPR retriever, and a hybrid-PPR variant whose ranking is carried by a PPR channel, on the first and held-out $200$-question splits of inference questions and the $200$-question compositional split. The largest swap effect on each kind of split is in \best {bold}}{table.caption.63}{}}
