\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces Inventory-transplant decomposition of the 2WikiMultiHop swap: reliable positive transfer depends on gold-derived passage links rather than lexical surface forms alone. Each row gives the mean paired hit@5 difference over the independent OpenIE KG, with its $10{,}000$-resample bootstrap $95\%$ CI. Transplant: the aligned KG's entity inventory transplanted into the OpenIE graph with its gold node-to-passage mapping intact. Mapping emptied: the same transplant with that mapping emptied. With the mapping intact, the transplant transfers a reliable share for PPR on both splits, with exact two-sided sign-test $p=9.1\times 10^{-4}$ and $p=3.1\times 10^{-5}$, and for the hybrid retriever on the first split, with $p=4.3\times 10^{-2}$. After the mapping is emptied, one nonsignificant positive effect of $+0.020$ remains, but all significant positive transfers disappear; the only CI excluding zero is negative. The largest transfer is in \textbf  {bold}.}}{34}{table.caption.64}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:transplant}{{24}{34}{Inventory-transplant decomposition of the 2WikiMultiHop swap: reliable positive transfer depends on gold-derived passage links rather than lexical surface forms alone. Each row gives the mean paired hit@5 difference over the independent OpenIE KG, with its $10{,}000$-resample bootstrap $95\%$ CI. Transplant: the aligned KG's entity inventory transplanted into the OpenIE graph with its gold node-to-passage mapping intact. Mapping emptied: the same transplant with that mapping emptied. With the mapping intact, the transplant transfers a reliable share for PPR on both splits, with exact two-sided sign-test $p=9.1\times 10^{-4}$ and $p=3.1\times 10^{-5}$, and for the hybrid retriever on the first split, with $p=4.3\times 10^{-2}$. After the mapping is emptied, one nonsignificant positive effect of $+0.020$ remains, but all significant positive transfers disappear; the only CI excluding zero is negative. The largest transfer is in \best {bold}}{table.caption.64}{}}
